            <ArticleTitle>Analysis of phasic flow velocity dynamics in the left anterior descending coronary artery before and after angioplasty using transthoracic echocardiography in patients with stable angina pectoris.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>614-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>High-frequency transthoracic Doppler echocardiography was used to determine the effects of significant stenosis on distal coronary blood flow velocity profiles. Before coronary angioplasty there was a reduction in diastolic and systolic flow and diastolic/systolic peak velocity ratio. After successful angioplasty velocity ratios returned to normal.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
